  "body": "Desktop PR **S0** of the webview arc (`specs/PR-DESKTOP-WEBVIEW-SPEC.md` §6.5) — contract **C7**. Version **6.41.3, PATCH**: a pure bug fix, no new surface, no new dependency, no shell.\n\n## The bug\n\n`uv tool uninstall` removes shims and nothing else. The config purge reaches only what is *inside* `~/.mcc` / `~/.fcc`. Every artefact the desktop half of an install writes lives outside both, so all of it survived an uninstall:\n\n* the Start Menu shortcut kept pointing at a deleted `mcc-desktop.exe` and did nothing when clicked;\n* the HKCU `Run` value — and on the other platforms the LaunchAgent, the systemd user unit and the XDG autostart entry — kept trying to launch a package that was no longer installed, at every login;\n* the `.desktop` entry, its icon and the macOS `.app` bundle stayed in the launcher forever.\n\n## Installer creates X → uninstaller removes it → test\n\n| Installer creates | Where | Uninstaller removes it | Test |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Start Menu shortcut (`New-DesktopShortcut`, `scripts/install.ps1:1096-1108`) | `%APPDATA%\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Start Menu\\Programs\\My Claude Code.lnk` | `scripts/uninstall.ps1:256` `Remove-StartMenuShortcut` (delete at `:284`) | `test_uninstallers.py::test_uninstall_ps1_removes_the_start_menu_shortcut` |\n| HKCU `Run` value (`_apply_windows_start_at_login`, `src/my_claude_code/config/desktop.py:528`; name at `:29`) | `HKCU:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run\\MyClaudeCodeDesktop` | `scripts/uninstall.ps1:300` `Remove-StartAtLoginRegistration` (delete at `:330`) | `test_uninstall_ps1_removes_the_start_at_login_registration` |\n| Shortcut icon (`scripts/install.ps1:1080`) | `~/.mcc/app-icon.ico` | already inside the purged config dir — `Purge-ConfigDir -DirName \".mcc\"` | parity row `Windows shortcut icon` |\n| `.desktop` entry (`create_linux_desktop_entry`, `scripts/install.sh:566`) | `~/.local/share/applications/my-claude-code.desktop` | `scripts/uninstall.sh:249` (`remove_desktop_launcher`) | `test_uninstall_sh_removes_every_desktop_artefact` |\n| `.desktop` icon (`scripts/install.sh:568`) | `~/.local/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps/my-claude-code.png` | `scripts/uninstall.sh:254` | same |\n| `.app` bundle (`create_macos_app_bundle`, `scripts/install.sh:603`) | `~/Applications/My Claude Code.app` | `scripts/uninstall.sh:255` (`rm -rf`, it is a directory) | same |\n| LaunchAgent plist (`_apply_macos_start_at_login`, `config/desktop.py:556`) | `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.myclaudecode.tray.plist` | `scripts/uninstall.sh:272` | same |\n| XDG autostart entry (`_apply_linux_start_at_login`, `config/desktop.py:587`) | `~/.config/autostart/mcc-server.desktop` | `scripts/uninstall.sh:271` | same |\n| systemd user unit (`_apply_linux_start_at_login`, `config/desktop.py:572`) | `~/.config/systemd/user/mcc-server.service` | `scripts/uninstall.sh:264-270` — `systemctl --user disable --now` first, then the file | same |\n\nEvery row is also enforced statically by `tests/contracts/test_uninstaller_parity.py::test_every_installer_created_artefact_is_removed_by_an_uninstaller`, which reads the *creating* file and the *removing* file and fails if either marker is gone. `test_every_artefact_row_names_a_creator_that_still_creates_it` keeps that table from going vacuous when an installer is refactored.\n\n## What is deliberately kept\n\nPurge semantics are untouched: `~/.mcc` and `~/.fcc` go, **`~/.fcc-old` stays** (it holds the user's rollback note), `~/.claude` is never touched, and uv, the uv-managed Python, Claude Code, Codex, Pi and shared `PATH` entries are left installed. `test_neither_uninstaller_touches_the_retired_rollback_directory` pins exactly that, so the new removals cannot drift into it. The shared XDG directories (`~/.local/share/applications`, `~/.config/autostart`) are left in place — they are not ours.\n\n## Safety properties preserved\n\n* **Ordering.** Desktop artefacts are removed only *after* every shim is verified gone, in the same gate that protects the config purge. An unverified tool removal now leaves config **and** shortcut exactly as they were (`test_uninstall_sh_keeps_desktop_artefacts_when_removal_is_unconfirmed`, `test_uninstall_ps1_keeps_the_shortcut_when_removal_is_unconfirmed`).\n* **`--dry-run` / `-DryRun`** prints each removal and performs none (two new scenarios).\n* **Best effort where it must be.** A `.lnk` the shell has open, or a locked `Run` key, warns rather than aborting — the tool and the config are already gone, so failing there would strand the user with nothing to retry (`test_uninstall_ps1_survives_a_registry_removal_failure`).\n* **Absence is normal.** The launcher is opt-in and autostart is off by default; a missing artefact is never an error, and `systemctl` is invoked only when the unit file we wrote is actually present, so a machine with no user bus is untouched.\n\n## Test-harness hardening (worth reviewing)\n\nThe PowerShell uninstaller fixture previously inherited the **real** `APPDATA` and had no registry stub. Adding shortcut and `Run`-value removal to the script without fixing that would have made a passing test delete the developer's own Start Menu entry and autostart value. The fixture now redirects `APPDATA`/`LOCALAPPDATA` into `tmp_path` (asserted in the fixture itself) and stubs `Get-ItemProperty` / `Remove-ItemProperty` in the wrapper, so no scenario in this suite can reach the real Start Menu or the real `Run` key.\n\n## Verification\n\n* Full suite on Windows: **9,176 passed**, 47 skipped, plus `tests/api/test_admin_static_jsdom.py` standalone **219 passed**. The 9 failures are the known local-only set (7 websearch/web-tools tests that read the real `~/.fcc/.env`, `test_catalog_publication_tracks_warm_refresh_and_direct_cache`); all are green on Linux CI.\n* `ruff format`, `ruff check`, `ty check` clean.\n* `scripts/uninstall.sh` was additionally driven end-to-end by hand under a redirected `HOME` with all six POSIX artefacts laid down (the POSIX fixture skips on Windows): every one was removed, the shared parent directories were left, and the call log showed exactly the expected `rm -rf` list.\n\n**Not verified here:** a real uninstall on this machine (the live server, its tray, its shortcut and its autostart were deliberately never touched); macOS behaviour on real hardware; and `systemctl --user disable` against a real user bus — CI has no session bus, so that branch is covered by the source contract and by the file-removal assertions only.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01JsSZ8AQXV1XKgKkgYBU5UT\n",
